Ionic bond strength is compared using Coulombic potential energy, which is proportional to \(q_1q_2/r\). Since the charges are identical,

\[
\frac{E_{\mathrm{NaCl}}}{E_{\mathrm{KF}}}
=\frac{r_{\mathrm{KF}}}{r_{\mathrm{NaCl}}}
=\frac{0.133+0.133}{0.097+0.181}
=\frac{0.266}{0.278}
\approx 0.9568=95.68\%.
\]

Thus (G) 95.6% is correct. Response B uses the appropriate inverse-distance dependence and reaches the gold answer; Response A incorrectly uses inverse-square dependence.

